      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my little boy is 13 months old and has a really bad fever, like 103.5. he's about 13kg. i have the infant acetaminophen (the 160mg per 5mL kind). i cant get ahold of the doctor and i'm really panicking because he's so miserable. i saw a guide online for high fevers that said for his weight we should be aiming for 15mg per kg to really get it under control. can you just do the math for me? i need to know exactly how many mL to put in the syringe so i know i'm giving him enough.",
